{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/75694-help-me-understand-mourners","id":75694,"title":"Help me understand Mourners","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-20T09:39:25-08:00","id":75694,"title":"Help me understand Mourners","content":"In general I love the Archetypes. I love the Jungian/Camusian vibe they give off, and their direct and polarizing natures. You can't walk away from death unchanged, whether you make a hard left from your previous life (a devout Mormon who, after surviving a terminal case of tuberculosis, abandons her faith, and becomes a hard-partying Celebrant) or continue on more-or-less the same course but with a deeper understanding of death, not to mention ghosty powers (a hypercritical academic who follows up a breakup with his boyfriend with a bathtub of ice, a bottle of rum, and a fistful of sleeping pills, only to realize at the last moment that he might be making a mistake, and now applies his cultural and philosophical research into the Underworld as a Necromancer).<br /> <br /> But right now I just don't see how Mourners fit into the scheme of things. Someone whose raison d'\u00eatre is essentially &quot;I shouldn't be alive right now&quot; doesn't seem like someone particularly cut out to be a Sin-Eater. What thought processes would drive a soul into the Mourner Archetype, and what do Mourners do? Hang out with ghosts and treat them as basically humans with some special needs? Found a mystery cult, envisaging herself as an avatar of death? Observe as many different kinds of death as he possibly can to figure out the perfect way to die? Hang out in graveyards and write gothic poetry? Use Manifestations to be as ghostlike as possible at all times?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T11:13:05-08:00","id":75745,"title":"","content":"Oh boy, this is an opportunity; my most-developed Sin-Eater character is a Mourner.* It's been several months since I worked with her, so some of this may be a little fuzzy, but\u2026<br /> <br /> Alice, as one of the Forgotten whose Threshold was achieved by being stabbed in the gut by someone not in his right mind, largely exemplifies her Archetype by playing up the persona of &quot;crazy death-witch who may find it more expedient at any time to murder you and interrogate your ghost,&quot; right down to deliberately sacrificing an eye to further empower her Aspect, but she's literally got some deathlord ancestry in her family tree and thinks of her krewe role as something like being the bride of a middling god, so she's a bit of an extreme example. On a more human note, a big reason she prefers dealing with the dead to dealing with regular people is the simple matter of heightened predictability and control - the context ritual provides is generally reassuring.<br /> <br /> A Mourner goes through their new life with the understanding that the person they used to be is gone - they have irrevocably changed, and that change includes being half-death. Their operative behavioral distinction is sort of a counterpoint to the Celebrants - where the Celebrants are all about celebrating life because you will die one day, the Mourners are about remembering death and the dead in the face of life's more evident aspects. They're the Bound who are most naturally inclined toward closeness to the dead, for all the different ways that can manifest.<br /> <br /> * &quot;I am apparently, and here I'm quoting some kook from the Network that I told about my first attempts, 'a natural' at the task of speaking words at the restless dead. With any luck she wasn't being sarcastic.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-20-2014, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T05:59:17-08:00","id":77611,"title":"","content":"&quot;The man I was before died in the accident; the thing standing before you is not human.&quot; I envision Mourners as being less &quot;I should've stayed dead&quot; and more &quot;I have become somethng else entirely.&quot; Expect them to raise their Synergy and Psyche faster than anyone else; becoming an avatar of death isn't a pleasant road to power for them, it consumes their existence. In their minds, they are dead, and the trappings of life are wasted on them. Better to oursue their new state with every fiber of their being. This might mean &quot;haunting&quot; the site of their death, or it could mean adopting a new persona and trying to embody that archetype in everything that they do (a la Avatars in Unknown Armies, if you're familiar).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}